)

\slide(
> Code and its results
```python
xs = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
print("mean:", sum(xs) / len(xs))
print("squares:", [x * x for x in xs])
```
// result_begin:
// mean: 3.0
// squares: [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]
// result_end

Run the block with C-c C-c. Its results are written under it, on the slide.
)

\slide(
> Notes and tips
\note(
A note reads the same on a slide as it does anywhere else.
)

\tip(
Fold a slide like any other block, or jump between slides from the outline.
)

